## 14.1 Synchronization Philosophy

PlinthOS is **offline-first** by design. The core principle is: **Local writes complete instantly** (<1ms), while network replication happens in the background. This eliminates the "spinning wheel" experience when network is unavailable.

### 14.1.1 Why CRDT?

Conflict-Free Replicated Data Types (CRDTs) enable:

| Benefit | Description |
|---|---|
| **No coordination required** | No central lock server; concurrent writes merge automatically |
| **Last-Writer-Wins (LWW)** for scalar values | Deterministic resolution without conflicts |
| **Add-Wins Set (OR-Set)** for collections | Elements added/removed; duplicates merged |
| **PN Counter** for integers | Increment/decrement; net count resolved deterministically |
| **Deterministic merge** | Any two replicas converging to same state after sync |

### 14.1.2 Sync Guarantees

| Guarantee | Description |
|---|---|
| **Convergence** | All replicas eventually reach same state |
| **Commutative operations** | Order of operations doesn't matter |
| **Idempotent** | Applying same mutation twice has no extra effect |
| **No single point of failure** | Any DO can accept mutations; replicates via D1 |

