## 14.2 CRDT Types Used in PlinthOS

PlinthOS uses three CRDT types from `packages/sync-protocol`:

### 14.2.1 LWW-Element-Set (Last-Writer-Wins Element Set)

**Used for**: Mutation envelopes, pending mutations list

| Operation | Effect |
|---|---|
| **Add**(`element`) | Adds element; timestamp tracks writer |
| **Remove**(`element`) | Marks element for removal; tombstoned if add wins |
| **Merge**(`R1`, `R2`) | Keeps element if either replica has it; winner determined by latest timestamp |

**Example**: `MutationEnvelope` set - ensures no duplicate mutations across replicas.

### 14.2.2 PN Counter (Positive-Negative Counter)

**Used for**: Stock level tracking, order item quantities, SLA timer counters

| Operation | Effect |
|---|---|
| **Increment**(`n`) | `p += n` |
| **Decrement**(`n`) | `n -= n` |
| **Merge**(`R1`, `R2`) | `p = max(p1 + p2_neg, p2 + p1_neg)` - net count |

**Example**: Stock `current_qty` - concurrent additions/decrements resolved deterministically.

### 14.2.3 OR-Set (Observed-Remove Set)

**Used for**: Menu item availability, modifier selections, 86'd items list

| Operation | Effect |
|---|---|
| **Add**(`element`, `observer`) | Adds element with observer ID |
| **Remove**(`element`, `observer`) | Removes only if observer added it |
| **Merge**(`R1`, `R2`) | Union of both; removes elements observers from both have removed |

**Example**: List of 86'd items per location - concurrent additions/removals merge without duplicates.

